      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t feel strong, but you can use `std::visit` to avoid deriving `std::variant` and defining the new member functions for `RingBlob`:\n\n```\nif (entry.ringBlob) {\n    std::visit([handle](auto\u0026\u0026 ringBlob) {\n        using T \u003d std::decay_t\u003cdecltype(ringBlob)\u003e;\n        if constexpr (std::is_same_v\u003cT, std::unique_ptr\u003cSharedMemory\u003e\u003e) {\n#ifdef _WIN32\n            handle-\u003eos_handle \u003d\n                static_cast\u003cint64_t\u003e(reinterpret_cast\u003cintptr_t\u003e(ringBlob-\u003ereleaseHandle()));\n#else\n            handle-\u003eos_handle \u003d static_cast\u003cint64_t\u003e(ringBlob-\u003ereleaseHandle());\n#endif\n            handle-\u003ehandle_type \u003d STREAM_MEM_HANDLE_TYPE_SHM;\n        }\n    }, *entry.ringBlob);\n}\n```",
